            question: "How do I know if brown grass is dead or just dormant?",
            answer: "Examine grass crowns at the soil line. Dormant grass has green or white crowns and remains anchored in soil - it will recover with proper water. Dead grass has brown, dried crowns, easily pulls from soil, and shows no green tissue. Dormant grass greens up within 1-2 weeks of resumed watering, while dead grass never recovers and needs reseeding or resodding."
